OL,3,GNEWSAGran 'shell shocked' at Black
OL,4,APudding Throwing world title
OL,5,
OL,6,FA grandmother has described being
OL,7,F"shell shocked" at becoming one of the
OL,8,Fjoint winners of the official Black
OL,9,FPudding Throwing World Championships.
OL,11,FJune Weir, 73, from Wilpshire,
OL,12,FLancashire, said she was delighted to
OL,13,Fbecome the first female to win the
OL,14,Fannual event at The Oak pub in
OL,15,FRamsbottom, Bury, on Sunday.
OL,17,FHundreds of people cheered on the
OL,18,Fthrowers as they hurled black puddings
OL,19,Fat Yorkshire puddings in the quirky
OL,20,Fsporting event, which first began more
OL,21,Fthan a century ago and raises money for
OL,22,Fcharity.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,410,400,260,160,0,100
